WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:04.790
Speaker 1: All right, I want to start today
with what's happening in the Israeli-Palestinian

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:10.720
conflict, where once again, we have another
major flare up and no clarity at this time

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:17.949
whether this will be on the order of weeks
or months in duration or possibly even longer.

00:00:17.949 --> 00:00:24.849
Now, normally, I would just jump right into
the story and what's going on and my perspective.

00:00:24.849 --> 00:00:32.500
But because of what I came into my office
to this morning, dozens and dozens of emails

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:38.770
and messages from people speculating as to
why I haven't talked about this yet, making

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:45.350
all sorts of accusations and allegations,
some of them very just sort of sad in terms

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:51.060
of what they imply people think is my life
on sort of a day to day basis.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:58.030
And I've not spoken about this recent flare
up much yet, only three times on a recent

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.300
bonus show and a couple of times on recent
live streams.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:05.600
I've not spoken much about it yet because
I've not felt that I have much to add or say.

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.079
That's different from my analysis the last
time we talked about it.

00:01:09.079 --> 00:01:14.509
But I received a couple of emails from longtime
viewers respectfully saying this feels like

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:17.469
it could be different this time and it would
be great for you to update your take on what's

00:01:17.469 --> 00:01:18.469
going on.

00:01:18.469 --> 00:01:19.639
And so I'm going to do it.

00:01:19.639 --> 00:01:26.979
I also received dozens of furious and often
emails playing on anti-Semitic tropes, referring

00:01:26.979 --> 00:01:31.899
to me as a Zionist Jew pig and things that
are even worse that I won't say because of

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:36.240
our radio affiliates so that they don't have
to bleep things.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:42.119
And people saying everything from you are
not talking about it because you're scared

00:01:42.119 --> 00:01:48.680
you'll be exposed as the Zionist pig that
you are or its financial reasons or whatever.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:54.469
So I'm under no illusion that those people
will be satisfied with this segment unless

00:01:54.469 --> 00:02:02.320
I unilaterally put the sole blame for a 70
year conflict at the hands of genocidal evil

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.320
Israel.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:08.099
And anyone who knows me knows I would never
give such childish black and white takes on

00:02:08.099 --> 00:02:09.099
any issue.

00:02:09.099 --> 00:02:13.630
And so those people who have been emailing
me saying I deserve to lose my show because

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:18.490
I haven't yet talked about it, I'm sure will
shift to saying I should lose my show because

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.430
of what I say today.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:22.410
This segment is not for them.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:27.530
Clearly, there were some really wacky things
being emailed to me, maybe on other platforms

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:28.530
as well.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.210
I've really only looked at emails, but maybe
things are crazy on the discord or on Reddit.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:36.360
I don't know people saying, well, clearly
I'm not saying anything because I'm afraid

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.090
of the blowback from from taking a position
my audience won't like.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.120
That's never stopped me before on the show.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.960
What I have said before is if there's an issue
that's unnecessarily inflammatory that most

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:50.900
of my audience seems not to care about, I
would consider skipping it.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:53.660
But I've done dozens of segments on the Israeli-Palestinian
conflict.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:59.680
Then I got email saying, David, you know,
you should really have the the courage to

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.170
do what this other Jewish person did and that
other Jewish person, they were able to put

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:10.290
aside their Jewish bias and take the correct
view on this, which is Israel is the only

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.830
problem in Israel in some cases even should
not exist, as some people emailed me.

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:17.310
David, why does your Judaism blind you?

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.310
You can't be a fair arbiter here because you're
Jewish.

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.780
This is the same argument that right wingers
made during the fight for gay rights, saying,

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.760
of course, gay people want gay marriage, they're
biased.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.570
You can't listen to them.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:33.350
They can't get past their personal connection
to the issue.

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:38.180
And it borders on anti-Semitic because it
plays on the trope of a dual loyalty that

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:42.990
American Jews have a conflicting loyalty to
Israel.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.760
Most Jews, of course, have never been to Israel.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.240
I've been there one six years ago.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.990
I don't live there.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:52.920
You won't be able to engage with me on things
like can't you put aside your Judaism and

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.720
take the correct position?

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.530
That's that's an identity politics rabbit
hole.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.530
It's trash.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:00.990
And I don't engage in that.

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:03.690
So I want to focus on what's been taking place.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.690
Now, one last thing.

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:09.000
And again, I hate that I even have to do this,
but you should see what I stepped into in

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.330
my inbox when I when I got in this morning.

00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:17.820
I also got email saying, David, you're motivated
by money, so you want to avoid losing money

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.070
if you give an unpopular take.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.710
And so that's why you're hiding your view
on the subject.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:26.360
And some people writing and saying, you know,
David, you used to cover the Israeli-Palestinian

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:29.560
conflict because you had a smaller audience
and you made less money.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.470
Now there's too much money at stake.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:37.180
I'm going to ignore for a second again the
anti-Semitic trope of Jews and money to say

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:41.720
that over time, as the show has been more
and more successful, financial considerations

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:45.090
are less and less a part of anything I do
at this point.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:48.840
I never chose stories based on money.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.970
I chose stories based on do I feel like talking
about it?

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:53.910
Do I feel like I have something to add?

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.280
Is this something my audience would be interested
in?

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.280
That's it.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.530
It's just my show and I pick this.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:03.980
Stories every day, financial incentives never
dictated story choice, they especially don't

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:09.280
right now, and by the way, if lots of people
are interested in the topic, then doing the

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:13.750
story would bring money no matter what I say,
hate watching is still watching.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.740
It still makes just as much money.

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:19.910
So it's not only an incorrect take, it's wrong
on the facts as well.

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:21.530
All of that now out of the way.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:25.640
All of the reasons why I've not been not doing
a story.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:27.210
Now out of the way.

00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.620
Let's talk about what's going on.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:32.870
And if you want to engage with me on this,
engage with what I'm actually saying.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:34.460
Not anything else that you're bringing in.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:41.640
OK, there are arguably two catalysts to this
flare up and both have Israel to blame.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:46.230
Both have Israel to blame, both have Israel
to blame.

00:05:46.230 --> 00:05:51.340
Can I find ways to maybe say the catalysts
are more to say?

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:53.990
I could, but they feel disingenuous to me.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.760
The narrow catalyst for this flare up is Israel.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:04.380
The first is that a squad of Israeli police
officers entered the Al-Aqsa Mosque in Jerusalem.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.300
This is a very volatile place.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.490
I was there a few years ago.

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:13.430
Non-Muslims are only allowed at Al-Aqsa during
certain time periods.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.440
Then I don't know what's going on now.

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.050
I was lucky to be there at just the right
time.

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:18.050
We were allowed in.

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:24.940
The Al-Aqsa Mosque is controlled by the Jordanian
authority within the old city of Jerusalem,

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:29.180
one of the most interesting places I've ever
been to the Old City in general and Al-Aqsa

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.810
itself, fascinating historical places.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:39.130
A squad of Israeli police officers entered
the Al-Aqsa Mosque in Jerusalem, brushed the

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:45.820
Palestinian Jordanian attendance aside, went
across the courtyard and cut the cables to

00:06:45.820 --> 00:06:52.260
loudspeakers that were broadcasting prayers
during Ramadan.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.260
Disastrous idea.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.550
Now, why did they do it?

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:57.680
The explanation is the Israeli president,
not prime minister.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:02.300
The Israeli president was delivering a speech
at the Western Wall on Israeli Memorial Day.

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:06.199
You had Ramadan prayers conflicting with a
Memorial Day speech.

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:08.500
So the speakers were cut to terrible idea.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:13.650
Now, you can argue and unfortunately, this
is how intractable this conflict is, where

00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:17.729
many of us would say, oh, come on, just, you
know, give this speech somewhere else or turn

00:07:17.729 --> 00:07:21.630
down the music or whatever that turned out
the prayers or whatever.

00:07:21.630 --> 00:07:23.280
That's not the way this conflict works.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:29.770
And if you've been following the 70 plus year
history of it, you would see why this explodes.

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:33.580
But I understand thinking what how is that?

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.170
What was the first catalyst then?

00:07:36.170 --> 00:07:41.720
We had the upcoming eviction of six families
from the Sheikh Jarrah neighborhood, a Palestinian

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:45.919
neighborhood in East Jerusalem that led the
protests.

00:07:45.919 --> 00:07:49.590
Then there was a police raid on the Al-Aqsa
Mosque on May 7th.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:55.080
Police officers with tear gas, stun grenades,
rubber bullets went into the mosque compound

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:57.669
around 8:00 p.m. local time.

00:07:57.669 --> 00:08:01.550
And this set off hours of clashes with protesters.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:05.190
There were hundreds of injuries, according
to medics that were on site, as reported by

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:06.580
The New York Times.

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:11.600
The police say that the stone throwers started
at worshipers are saying the Israeli police

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:14.600
started it and then things exploded.

00:08:14.600 --> 00:08:20.810
As usual, each side has their own view on
who the real wrongdoers are and who is merely

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:28.400
reacting to the other side, another intractable
bedrock of every single one of these flare

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:29.460
ups.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.570
And there's plenty to go around.

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:36.001
Dozens and dozens of Hamas rockets coming
over from Gaza, even reaching Tel Aviv, Israel

00:08:36.001 --> 00:08:40.419
doing bombings, as is always the case, Israel's
actions leading to more death.

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:45.280
Now, let me say one thing about this whole
disproportionate response thing that often

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:46.490
is is mentioned.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.970
Yes, Israel's response is disproportionate.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.810
That's absolutely true.

00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:55.060
Israel is far better armed than the Hamas
terrorists in Gaza.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.880
That's absolutely true.

00:08:56.880 --> 00:09:02.860
And whenever this happens, there tend to be
more deaths as a result of Israeli action.

00:09:02.860 --> 00:09:05.690
That's absolutely true and that's horrible.

00:09:05.690 --> 00:09:11.210
I think that we should also be honest with
ourselves that some of the people who say,

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:18.100
well, if six Palestinians die and one Israeli
dies, it's a disproportionate response.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:21.430
I don't think they would be pleased if the
numbers were the same.

00:09:21.430 --> 00:09:27.800
I mean, would we really be seeing a different
reaction from people if 12 Palestinians and

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:31.670
12 Israelis died, would then would that no
longer be a factor?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:32.710
I don't think so.

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:35.910
So, of course, the response is disproportionate.

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:40.880
Disproportionate responses are a common thing
in many conflicts, ethnic, political, military,

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:41.900
et cetera.

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:47.339
It doesn't mean it's good, but to focus on
that when obviously the side that's better

00:09:47.339 --> 00:09:52.580
armed is likely to do more damage, I don't
think it helps us understand what's going

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:55.390
on any better now than Israel did.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:59.160
Another completely harebrained thing, blowing
up a building in which the Associated Press

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.360
was working in Gaza saying there were Hamas
there.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:07.560
Now, maybe there were Hamas, maybe they weren't.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:12.350
Israeli authorities did call and say, get
out because we're going to hit this building.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:16.550
Whatever is the case, Hamas is in all sorts
of different places.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:22.600
And it just seems idiotic to me to target
this building because it does exactly what

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:27.610
Israel's opponents want to say Israel does,
which is suppress criticism and news of what's

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:28.620
happening in Gaza.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.800
And in some literal sense, that's exactly
what happens when you will.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:36.690
Blow up a building out of which the AP is
working, a disastrous idea, absolutely condemnable.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:40.260
So let's go through these things first and
I'll tell you where I stand and pay close

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:44.850
attention, because, again, I'm not going to
engage in responses that mischaracterize what

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:52.180
I say I am and have been against evictions
and settlements, period, for the 25 years

00:10:52.180 --> 00:10:54.550
I've been following this conflict.

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:57.290
There's no there's no mitigator.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:58.730
I'm just I'm against it.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:00.290
I condemn it.

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:04.750
This current Israeli government makes me sick
and has for a long time.

00:11:04.750 --> 00:11:06.660
And settlements are a big part of that.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:11.770
One thing that is important and that tons
of people are missing are that much like the

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:17.709
Palestinian people are different from Hamas
and the Palestinian Authority and the ultra

00:11:17.709 --> 00:11:22.740
radical Palestinians, the Israeli people,
Israel as a country and the current administration

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.220
are three different things.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:30.230
When during the Iraq war years, some Europeans
wrongly saw all Americans as war mongers who

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:34.370
wanted to go to Iraq, we all understood why
that didn't make sense.

00:11:34.370 --> 00:11:37.760
We know the difference intuitively between
the Trump administration, the United States

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.820
as a country and Americans as individuals.

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:45.149
And yet more than half the emails I received
about this don't seem to understand or make

00:11:45.149 --> 00:11:51.130
that distinction between the Netanyahu administration,
Israel as a country and the Israeli people

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:53.589
using the three terms interchangeably.

00:11:53.589 --> 00:11:56.480
And that's just a fundamental misunderstanding
of what's going on.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:00.310
How can we even have a remotely sensible conversation
about this conflict?

00:12:00.310 --> 00:12:06.880
If you interchangeably assign blame or characterize
three separate entities, the current administration,

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:10.920
Israel as a country and the Israeli people
as one one in the same, the evictions from

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:15.700
East Jerusalem are at the heart of this, and
I'm 100 percent against that.

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:18.670
They are illegal by international law, period.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.220
Settlers are radical extremists.

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:22.010
I share nothing with them.

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.640
I am diametrically opposed.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:29.440
Settlers are a tiny fraction of Israeli Jews
who are just a portion of world Jews.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:35.899
Unless someone says I'm for the settlements,
I assume that they are not because this is

00:12:35.899 --> 00:12:39.770
such a radical and relatively fringe group.

00:12:39.770 --> 00:12:43.399
Settlers are, in a sense, massive provocateurs,
shameless ones at that.

00:12:43.399 --> 00:12:50.250
And sadly, right now, the Netanyahu government
is benefiting from the settlers and so they

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.830
are allowing this to happen.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:57.630
Second, I am 100 percent against the Netanyahu
government, which I believe is allowing this

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:02.990
to happen for the benefit of Benjamin Netanyahu,
the depraved and disgusting right wing Prime

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:06.410
Minister Netanyahu knows his days are numbered.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:08.020
He was unable to form a government.

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:11.920
So he is allowing this to happen now because
this is how he operates.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:12.920
Look at the chaos.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:13.920
You need me.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:16.360
He pulled this before an election some years
ago.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:21.830
Now, this is when maybe some people want me
to start saying who is to blame and to what

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:22.830
degree.

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:29.459
David, police say this conflict is 99 percent
Israel or say it's all Hamas or you are a

00:13:29.459 --> 00:13:31.420
Hamas sympathizer.

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:33.170
Nothing is that simple.

00:13:33.170 --> 00:13:38.450
What I will tell you is what I see as the
most likely path to peace for the long term.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:44.990
And it requires both Netanyahu and Likud not
to be in power on the Israeli side and somehow

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:50.550
for Hamas to be removed from power in Gaza,
but not replaced by Hezbollah, which is essentially

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.450
as bad but better armed.

00:13:52.450 --> 00:13:53.740
So here's my perspective.

00:13:53.740 --> 00:13:58.660
If you said what is the most likely path to
peace, and this is why I didn't have much

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:05.050
to say initially in this, because fundamentally
the path to peace has not changed, in my view.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:10.380
So starting with the big picture, anyone who
thinks that there should be no Palestinian

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:14.110
state in the future is just not a productive
participant here.

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:19.820
The Palestinians need a state of their own,
a contiguous one, which I will get to.

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:24.899
Anyone who thinks there should be no country
of Israel is also not a productive participant.

00:14:24.899 --> 00:14:29.850
And if you really want to see a situation
where many people would die, it would be an

00:14:29.850 --> 00:14:36.600
a real attempt, but by serious players to
make Israel no longer a country.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:41.510
So the Palestinian people deserve a state
and to live in peace and the Israeli people

00:14:41.510 --> 00:14:42.670
do as well.

00:14:42.670 --> 00:14:47.790
And right now, neither side is being led by
those who benefit from peace or who want it.

00:14:47.790 --> 00:14:49.500
Until that changes, nothing will change.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:55.420
So the first question is, who's in charge
in a hypothetical peaceful situation in Israel?

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:59.149
It's not Netanyahu and it's not Likud.

00:14:59.149 --> 00:15:04.980
OK, on the Palestinian side, Hamas must be
replaced by a more secular Palestinian Authority

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:05.980
immediately.

00:15:05.980 --> 00:15:10.370
Hezbollah replacing Hamas won't get us to
serious peace possibilities.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:14.360
Does Mahmoud Abbas have a role to play there,
currently overseeing the West Bank?

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:15.490
Maybe I'm open to that.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.579
It doesn't seem Hamas is open to that.

00:15:17.579 --> 00:15:21.170
When you look at how long Abbas has been around,
I think you can also increasingly make the

00:15:21.170 --> 00:15:25.850
case that Abbas is not a likely arbiter to
a longer term peace.

00:15:25.850 --> 00:15:29.670
Abbas has also given lie riddled speeches
at the U.N.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.540
So has Benjamin Netanyahu to.

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:36.490
To the extent that Abbas might be a productive
partner, I'm open to it being a Mahmoud Abbas

00:15:36.490 --> 00:15:43.560
led a coalition government, West Bank and
Gaza, but I don't know how feasible that really

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:45.560
is.

00:15:45.560 --> 00:15:51.860
In all likelihood, you are going to need to
have the law of return for Jews to Israel

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:58.190
maintained and a law overturn established
for the future Palestinian state.

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:03.670
Now, the entire point of Israel is since Jews
were kicked out and discriminated of so many

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:08.250
parts of the world for so long, that's a place
Jews know they can go.

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:13.290
Even if Hungary turn turns extremely right
wing, anti-Semitic or anti-Semitic or whatever

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:14.980
the case may be.

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:22.460
There also is going to have to be, I believe,
some ability for Palestinians to return to

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:23.800
Israel.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:27.290
Something is going to have to be conceded
mathematically.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.300
And this is something Yasser Arafat talked
about in the 90s.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:32.460
It's not going to be five million Palestinians.

00:16:32.460 --> 00:16:34.120
It's just not going to happen.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:40.300
So we need a combination of some reasonable
Palestinian return to what will be the state

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:41.500
of Israel.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:49.000
Certainly the Palestinian state will be able
to decide who is allowed to go there as well.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:53.710
Anyone who wants to move back to Gaza or the
West Bank would be free to do so if the Palestinian

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:55.389
Authority wants to allow it.

00:16:55.389 --> 00:17:02.180
Now, Ehud Barak in the past proposed a symbolic
number of Palestinian return to Israel and

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:05.000
significant financial reparations.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.300
That's something that could be looked at.

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:14.470
But but that's more details once we get past
sort of the big questions in terms of the

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:16.049
land, what are the borders?

00:17:16.049 --> 00:17:17.049
Right.

00:17:17.049 --> 00:17:24.230
I believe the most likely path to peace will
come with something that is more or less the

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:29.501
Clinton proposed borders or similar, which
is similar to a lot of the recent ideas, not

00:17:29.501 --> 00:17:30.501
the Trump ideas.

00:17:30.501 --> 00:17:31.501
Forget Trump Trump.

00:17:31.501 --> 00:17:35.230
Anything Trump said is in the trash of the
Palestinian territory would include the West

00:17:35.230 --> 00:17:36.770
Bank, Gaza and East Jerusalem.

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:38.960
Yes, East Jerusalem.

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:43.070
There are some problems with exactly what
the limits of East Jerusalem would be because

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:44.100
they are disputed.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:48.660
But let's imagine if we got to this point,
they could be agreed upon.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:52.120
East Jerusalem would become the capital of
the Palestinian state.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:54.430
I think that has to be conceded.

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:59.650
And the caveat would be the Jewish quarter
of East Jerusalem should remain under Israeli

00:17:59.650 --> 00:18:00.650
sovereignty.

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:02.330
We could do just a whole show on this.

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:06.480
But if you look at the desecration of the
Jewish quarter when it was not under Israeli

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:10.590
control from, I believe, forty nine to sixty
seven, you can read more about that.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:13.400
I think that is a caveat on settlements.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:17.600
I mean, just all settlements have to stop
immediately.

00:18:17.600 --> 00:18:24.080
Israel has to agree in principle to remove
settlements that can be removed and to offer

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.580
meaningful land swaps for those that cannot.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:31.570
Now, as a practical reality and I also go
back to what Arafat said about this, not all

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:34.090
the settlements at this point can be realistically
removed.

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.090
I hate that.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:36.970
That's disgusting.

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:40.480
But if you say, David, you're the pragmatist
negotiator.

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:43.620
Morally, I have no problem with removing every
settlement.

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.940
And I know the talking point is, well, these
are people's homes.

00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:46.940
Yes.

00:18:46.940 --> 00:18:50.390
They're people's homes that were built in
violation of international law and they never

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:51.880
should have been built.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:59.299
Yasser Arafat had the idea that keeping the
larger settlements in exchange for meaningful

00:18:59.299 --> 00:19:02.150
land swaps would be OK.

00:19:02.150 --> 00:19:05.960
That's probably something that would would
have to be negotiated.

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:12.010
And then certainly, on the other hand, you
know, all all settlements have to stop.

00:19:12.010 --> 00:19:15.190
I believe the blockade has to be lifted to
Gaza.

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:24.080
You do have to have some way of preventing
weapon materials from being brought in.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:25.320
It has to be negotiated.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.910
But the blockade as a sign of good faith,
at least initially, has to be lifted.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:34.480
Of course, Palestinians have to immediately
all Palestinian groups have to stop all rockets

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:38.640
immediately stop the tunnel building, so on
and so forth.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:43.980
Hamas and other groups have to demilitarize
Gaza as part of a peace agreement we saw in

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:48.070
the two year period after the withdrawal of
Israel from Gaza, but before the blockade

00:19:48.070 --> 00:19:50.900
was put in place, you know, thousands of rockets.

00:19:50.900 --> 00:19:54.900
So there has to be a demilitarization, but
the Gaza blockade has to be removed.

00:19:54.900 --> 00:19:59.929
And as long as the demilitarization and no
rockets are held to the deal, the blockade

00:19:59.929 --> 00:20:01.280
has to be removed.

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:02.910
How do you hold people to that?

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:03.910
I don't know.

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.100
That has to be figured out.

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:11.559
And then lastly, the eventual peace agreement
has to include that all claims are being renounced

00:20:11.559 --> 00:20:17.200
and it is the end of the conflict period,
because the problem you run into is you have

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:22.690
some sort of an agreement in principle, but
not all claims are renounced.

00:20:22.690 --> 00:20:28.440
And then when the agreement is violated, everybody
goes back to pretending like this was never

00:20:28.440 --> 00:20:30.539
identified as the end of the conflict.

00:20:30.539 --> 00:20:31.539
If there's.

00:20:31.539 --> 00:20:34.910
Going to be a serious deal once the right
players come to the table, and as I already

00:20:34.910 --> 00:20:37.630
mentioned, who those are is complicated.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.660
It has to be determined that that is the end
of the conflict.

00:20:41.660 --> 00:20:46.370
And in the future, that allows any violator
of the agreement, either on the Israeli or

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:49.360
the Palestinian side to be held to account.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:52.700
Some non-binding thing is not going to get
us what we need.

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:59.210
If you want to react, address the specific
points, all insults, anti-Semitic responses,

00:20:59.210 --> 00:21:02.650
blanket replies, like what I had over the
weekend in my email, Zionist pig.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.700
It's all going to be ignored.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:12.500
The winners here are Netanyahu and Hamas,
chaos from which Netanyahu can say, you need

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.270
me to protect you.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:15.600
That's a gift.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:20.760
Hamas justified in its brutal grip on the
Gazan people because look at what Israel is

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:21.760
doing to us.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:26.260
We're the only ones who can respond with the
rockets the Palestinian people lose here.

00:21:26.260 --> 00:21:30.150
The Israeli people lose, Bibi wins and Hamas
wins.

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:31.530
I look forward to hearing your thoughts.

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:32.530
